# Đề bài

- a) Cho $\cos \alpha = \dfrac{3}{4}$ với $0^{\circ} < \alpha < 90^{\circ}$. Tính $A = \dfrac{\tan \alpha + 3 \cot \alpha}{\tan \alpha + \cot \alpha}$.
- b) Cho $\tan \alpha = \sqrt{2}$. Tính $B = \dfrac{\sin \alpha - \cos \alpha}{\sin^3 \alpha + 3 \cos^3 \alpha + 2 \sin \alpha}$.

# Lời giải

- a) Ta có $A = \dfrac{\tan \alpha + 3 \cdot \dfrac{1}{\tan \alpha}}{\tan \alpha + \dfrac{1}{\tan \alpha}} = \dfrac{\dfrac{\tan^2 \alpha + 3}{\tan \alpha}}{\dfrac{\tan^2 \alpha + 1}{\tan \alpha}} = \dfrac{\tan^2 \alpha + 3}{\tan^2 \alpha + 1} = 1 + 2 \cos^2 \alpha$.
Suy ra $A = 1 + 2 \cdot \dfrac{9}{16} = \dfrac{25}{16} = \dfrac{17}{8}$.

- b) Ta có 
$$
B = \dfrac{\sin \alpha - \cos \alpha}{\dfrac{\cos^3 \alpha}{\cos^3 \alpha} + \dfrac{\sin \alpha}{\cos^3 \alpha}} = \dfrac{\tan \alpha \left(\tan^2 \alpha + 1\right) - \left(\tan^2 \alpha + 1\right)}{\tan^3 \alpha + 3 + 2 \tan \alpha \left(\tan^2 \alpha + 1\right)}
$$
$$
\text{Suy ra } B = \dfrac{\sqrt{2}\left(2 + 1\right) - \left(2 + 1\right)}{2\sqrt{2} + 3 + 2\sqrt{2} \cdot \left(2 + 1\right)} = \dfrac{3 \left(\sqrt{2} - 1\right)}{3 + 5 \sqrt{2}}.
$$

