# Đề bài

Cho $a, b$ là các số dương và thỏa mãn hệ thức $\dfrac{\sin^4x}{a}+\dfrac{\cos^4x}{b}=\dfrac{1}{a+b}$. 
Chứng minh rằng $\dfrac{\sin^{2018}x}{a^{1008}}+\dfrac{\cos^{2018}x}{b^{1008}}=\dfrac{1}{(a+b)^{1008}}.$

# Lời giải

Ta có
$$
\dfrac{\sin^4x}{a}+\dfrac{\cos^4x}{b}=\dfrac{1}{a+b}\Leftrightarrow (a+b)\left(\dfrac{\sin^4x}{a}+\dfrac{\cos^4x}{b}\right)=1
\Leftrightarrow (a+b)\left(\dfrac{\sin^4x}{a}+\dfrac{\cos^4x}{b}\right)=\left(\sin^2x+\cos^2x\right)^2
\Leftrightarrow \dfrac{a}{b}\cos^4x+\dfrac{b}{a}\sin^4x-2\sin^2x\cos^2x=0
\Leftrightarrow \left(\sqrt{\dfrac{b}{a}}\cos^2x-\sqrt{\dfrac{a}{b}}\sin^2x\right)^2=0
\Leftrightarrow \sqrt{\dfrac{b}{a}}\cos^2x=\sqrt{\dfrac{a}{b}}\sin^2x
\Leftrightarrow \dfrac{\sin^2x}{a}=\dfrac{\cos^2x}{b}.
$$
Từ đó suy ra $\dfrac{\sin^2x}{a}=\dfrac{\cos^2x}{b}=\dfrac{1}{a+b}>0$.
Đặt $t=\dfrac{1}{a+b}\Rightarrow\begin{cases}\sin^2x=at\\\cos^2x=bt\end{cases}$, do đó ta có $\begin{cases}\sin^{2018}x=a^{1009}t^{1009}\\\cos^{2018}x=b^{1009}t^{1009}\end{cases}.$
Vậy $\dfrac{\sin^{2018}x}{a^{1008}}+\dfrac{\cos^{2012}x}{b^{1008}}=\dfrac{a^{1009}t^{1009}}{a^{1008}}+\dfrac{b^{1009}t^{1009}}{b^{1008}}=(a+b)t^{1009}=\dfrac{1}{(a+b)^{1008}}.$

