# Đề bài

Đơn giản biểu thức sau

1) $A=\sin{30^{\circ}}\cdot\cos{60^{\circ}}+\sin{60^{\circ}}\cdot\cos{30^{\circ}}$.

2) $B=\sin{\alpha}+\cos{\alpha}\cdot\tan{\alpha}$.

3) $C=\dfrac{2\cos^2{x}-1}{\sin{x}+\cos{x}}$.

4) $D=(\tan{x}-\cot{x})^2-(\tan{x}+\cot{x})^2 $.

# Lời giải

1) Vì $30^{\circ}$ và $60^{\circ}$ là hai góc phụ nhau nên
* $\sin{30^{\circ}}=\cos{60^{\circ}}$.
* $\sin{60^{\circ}}=\cos{30^{\circ}}$.

Suy ra $A=\sin{30^{\circ}}\cdot\cos{60^{\circ}}+\sin{60^{\circ}}\cdot\cos{30^{\circ}}=\cos^2{60^{\circ}}+\sin^2{60^{\circ}}=1$.

2) Ta có
$$B=\sin{\alpha}+\cos{\alpha}\tan{\alpha}=\sin{\alpha}+\cos{\alpha}\cdot\dfrac{\sin{\alpha}}{\cos{\alpha}}=2\sin{\alpha}.$$
Vậy $B=2\sin{\alpha}$.

3) Ta có
$$C=\dfrac{2\cos^2{x}-1}{\sin{x}+ \cos{x}} =\dfrac{\cos^2{x}-\sin^2{x}}{\sin{x}+\cos{x}} =\cos{x}-\sin{x}.$$
Vậy $C=\cos{x}-\sin{x}$.

4) Ta có
$$
\begin{aligned}
D&=(\tan{x}-\cot{x})^2-(\tan{x}+\cot{x})^2\\
&=\tan^2{x}-2\tan{x}\cot{x}+\cot^2{x}-\tan^2{x}-2\tan{x}\cot{x}-\cot^2{x}\\
&=-4\tan{x}\cot{x}\\
&=-4\ (\text{do }\ \tan{x}\cot{x}=1).
\end{aligned}
$$
Vậy $D=-4$.

