# Đề bài

Chứng rằng các biểu thức sau có giá trị không phụ thuộc vào $x$.

1) $A=\sin^8x+\sin^6x\cos^2x+\sin^4x\cos^2x+\sin^2x\cos^2x+\cos^2x$.

2) $B=\dfrac{1-\sin^6x}{\cos^6x}-\dfrac{3\tan^2x}{\cos^2x}$.

# Lời giải

1) Ta có 
$$
\begin{aligned}
A&=\sin^8x+\sin^6x\cos^2x+\sin^4x\cos^2x+\sin^2x\cos^2x+\cos^2x \\
&=\sin^6x\left(\sin^2x+\cos^2x\right)+\sin^4x\cos^2x+\sin^2x\cos^2x+\cos^2x \\
&=\sin^6x+\sin^4x\cos^2x+\sin^2x\cos^2x+\cos^2x \\
&=\sin^4x\left(\sin^2x+\cos^2x\right)+\sin^2x\cos^2x+\cos^2x \\
&=\sin^4x+\sin^2x\cos^2x+\cos^2x \\
&=\sin^2x\left(\sin^2x+\cos^2x\right)+\cos^2x \\
&=\sin^2x+\cos^2x =1.
\end{aligned}
$$

2) Điều kiện $\cos x\neq 0$.
$$
\begin{aligned}
B&=\dfrac{1-\sin^6x}{\cos^6x}-\dfrac{3\tan^2x}{\cos^2x}
=\dfrac{1-\sin^6x}{\cos^6x}-\dfrac{3\sin^2x}{\cos^4x} \\
&=\dfrac{1-\sin^6x}{\cos^6x}-\dfrac{3\sin^2x\cos^2x}{\cos^6x}
=\dfrac{1-\sin^6x-3\sin^2x\cos^2x}{\cos^6x}\\
&=\dfrac{\left(1-\sin^2x\right)^3+3\sin^2x(1-\sin^2x)-3\sin^2x\cos^2x}{\cos^6x}\\
&=\dfrac{\left(\cos^2x\right)^3+3\sin^2x\cos^2x-3\sin^2x\cos^2x}{\cos^6x}\\
&=\dfrac{\cos^6x}{\cos^6x}
=1.
\end{aligned}
$$

